0..110 Comment "/// This source checks pairs against definitions whose dependent record types reach a record type over a call."
111..114 Comment "///"
115..232 Comment "/// It pins how the kernel replays the unfoldings of those definitions: its own δ-step against the checker\'s reduct."
233..236 Comment "///"
237..478 Comment "/// Each record type sits behind a stuck arm over the outer record\'s first field. The checker\'s reduct runs the call inside the record type. The kernel\'s δ-step holds it, and the kernel reads the two codes alike once it reads their decodes."
479..482 Comment "///"
483..499 Comment "/// - see: #3045"
500..516 Comment "/// - see: #2831"
